OL,3,ASir Ranulph Fiennes' relatives tell BBC
OL,4,Ait's 'very painful' not being able to
OL,5,Avisit him
OL,6,
OL,7,FRelatives of the British explorer Sir
OL,8,FRanulph Fiennes have said it is "very
OL,9,Fpainful" he appears to have been hidden
OL,10,Faway from them.
OL,12,FSpeaking to BBC Newsnight, his former
OL,13,Fsister-in-law told the BBC that she did
OL,14,Fnot know where he was, and nobody had
OL,15,Fbeen able to see him.
OL,17,FIt has been alleged that Sir Ranulph,
OL,18,F82, has been admitted to a number of
OL,19,Fcare homes under assumed names, after a
OL,20,Ffamily rift involving his second wife,
OL,21,FLouise Millington-Cotes.
OL,23,APub: 29-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBCultureC Nat RadioFTechnology
FL,171,160,200,105,0,100
